  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between AC-262536 and Aldo-keto reductase family 1 member C3, mediated through ligandrol, which appears to be a common target of AC-262536 in multiple pathways. The core mechanism appears to involve ligandrol acting as a target of AC-262536, with the Aldo-keto reductase family 1 member C3 being a downstream target of ligandrol. This indicates a possible pathway where AC-262536 modulates ligandrol's activity, which in turn affects the Aldo-keto reductase family 1 member C3. The consistent scores across the three paths suggest a robust, mechanistically plausible link, particularly given the shared role of ligandrol as a common target in these relationships. The presence of multiple independent pathways reinforcing this connection supports the hypothesis that AC-262536 may influence the activity of ligandrol, which then impacts the Aldo-keto reductase family 1 member C3. The evidence does not provide direct evidence of AC-262536's direct interaction with Aldo-keto reductase family 1 member C3, but rather through ligandrol, which strengthens the mechanistic link.",
